  "claim_boundary": "This v3 study is a non-overlapping source-test replication and a trajectory-level transport-calibration analysis. The exact v2 result, source revision, workflow run, artifact digest, fixed operating point, and source-test filenames are bound before replication. The replication test rosters must have zero filename overlap with that exact v2 source-test roster. The additive transport slack is calibrated only from complete calibration trajectories and targets trajectory-mean normalized regret under a trajectory-exchangeability assumption; it is not a per-decision safety guarantee. The split domain was selected using filenames only, not trajectory outcomes. Official DEFORM evaluation files remain absent. This is not unseen-object validation, learned-sensor validation, continuous-control certification, deployment safety, or state of the art."
